  "term": "ABPP",
  "definition": "ABPP refers to amyloid-beta precursor protein, a human protein made from the APP gene. It helps with receptor-related signaling at the cell surface and can be cut into several smaller products, including soluble peptides, membrane-bound fragments, components of amyloid plaques, regulatory molecules, and neurotoxic fragments.",
